READING THIS PAGE
-----------------
Nothing here depends on color; every reading is in words.
SFI (solar flux): Sun's 10.7 cm radio output; higher opens the upper HF bands.
  Band verdicts follow N0NBH (hamqsl.com); NOAA publishes the raw number.
Sunspot number: daily sunspot count; rises and falls with the 11-year cycle.
Kp: how disturbed Earth's field is, 0 (calm) to 9 (extreme). 5+ is a storm.
Solar wind / Bz: particle stream and its field tilt; Bz at -5 nT or lower
  (southward) drives storms; northward keeps things quiet.
Times are UTC.
